{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' openspec/changes/lint-audit-skill/specs/config-apply/spec.md\"","aggregated_output":"## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: Offer per-item and batch apply modes\nThe skill SHALL offer three apply modes after presenting the report.\n\n#### Scenario: Apply all\n- **WHEN** the user chooses \"apply all\"\n- **THEN** the skill applies every missing recommendation (oxlint rules, tsconfig settings, and type-aware linting enablement) without further prompts\n\n#### Scenario: Skip all\n- **WHEN** the user chooses \"skip all\"\n- **THEN** the skill exits without making any changes\n\n#### Scenario: Per-item review\n- **WHEN** the user chooses \"review per-item\"\n- **THEN** the skill presents each missing recommendation individually with accept/deny, applying only the accepted ones\n\n### Requirement: Apply oxlint rule changes to JSON config\nThe skill SHALL create or update `.oxlintrc.json` when applying oxlint rule recommendations.\n\n#### Scenario: Create new config\n- **WHEN** no oxlint config exists and the user accepts oxlint rule recommendations\n- **THEN** the skill creates `.oxlintrc.json` at the project root with the accepted rules\n\n#### Scenario: Update existing JSON config\n- **WHEN** `.oxlintrc.json` exists and the user accepts additional rules\n- **THEN** the skill adds the accepted rules to the existing config's `rules` object without removing existing rules\n\n#### Scenario: JSONC config format\n- **WHEN** `.oxlintrc.jsonc` exists and the user accepts additional rules\n- **THEN** the skill prints the rule configuration as JSON that the user can manually add, and does NOT modify the `.jsonc` file (JSONC comment preservation is fragile)\n\n#### Scenario: TypeScript config format\n- **WHEN** `oxlint.config.ts` is the active config and the user accepts rules\n- **THEN** the skill prints the rule configuration as JSON that the user can manually add, and does NOT modify the `.ts` file\n\n### Requirement: Apply tsconfig strictness changes\nThe skill SHALL update tsconfig.json files when applying strictness recommendations.\n\n#### Scenario: Enable strict mode\n- **WHEN** the user accepts the `strict` recommendation for a specific tsconfig\n- **THEN** the skill adds `\"strict\": true` to `compilerOptions` in that tsconfig\n\n#### Scenario: Enable noUncheckedIndexedAccess\n- **WHEN** the user accepts the `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` recommendation\n- **THEN** the skill adds `\"noUncheckedIndexedAccess\": true` to `compilerOptions`\n\n#### Scenario: Enable erasableSyntaxOnly\n- **WHEN** the user accepts the `erasableSyntaxOnly` recommendation\n- **THEN** the skill adds `\"erasableSyntaxOnly\": true` to `compilerOptions`\n\n#### Scenario: Show migration scope before applying strictness settings\n- **WHEN** the user is reviewing `strict`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, or `erasableSyntaxOnly` in per-item mode\n- **THEN** the skill shows the error count for that specific setting before asking for accept/deny\n\n### Requirement: Recommend type-aware linting enablement\nThe skill SHALL recommend enabling type-aware linting when it is not active.\n\n#### Scenario: Recommend --type-aware flag\n- **WHEN** oxlint is installed but type-aware linting is not enabled\n- **THEN** the skill recommends adding `--type-aware` to the project's lint script and shows the exact command modification needed\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"tool_end","dispatch_id":"01KSY183A9RB4MC0YNZAXNDH3H","ts":"2026-05-31T03:29:41Z","tool":"command_execution"}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '261,520p' skills/lint-audit/audit.sh\"","aggregated_output":"  type_aware_config=$(jq -r '\n    [\n      .. | objects\n      | if has(\"typeAware\") then .typeAware\n        elif has(\"type_aware\") then .type_aware\n        elif has(\"type-aware\") then .\"type-aware\"\n        else empty\n        end\n    ]\n    | any(. == true or . == \"true\" or . == \"enabled\" or . == \"on\")\n  ' \"$config_json\")\nfi\n\nif [ \"$type_aware_script\" = \"true\" ] || [ \"$type_aware_config\" = \"true\" ]; then\n  type_aware=true\nelse\n  type_aware=false\nfi\n\ntsconfig_list=\"${tmp_dir}/tsconfigs.txt\"\n(\n  cd \"$project_abs\"\n  find . \\( -path './*/*/*/*' -prune \\) -o -type f -name 'tsconfig*.json' -print\n) | sed 's#^\\./##' | sort >\"$tsconfig_list\"\n\ntsconfig_items=\"${tmp_dir}/tsconfig-items.jsonl\"\n: >\"$tsconfig_items\"\nhas_tsc=true\nif ! command -v tsc >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  has_tsc=false\nfi\n\nsetting_rationale() {\n  case \"$1\" in\n    strict) printf '%s\\n' \"Enable strict TypeScript checking so agents cannot lean on weak inferred types.\" ;;\n    noUncheckedIndexedAccess) printf '%s\\n' \"Require undefined handling for indexed access instead of assuming keys exist.\" ;;\n    erasableSyntaxOnly) printf '%s\\n' \"Keep TypeScript syntax erasable so runtime behavior stays explicit.\" ;;\n    *) printf '%s\\n' \"\" ;;\n  esac\n}\n\nwhile IFS= read -r tsconfig_path; do\n  [ -n \"$tsconfig_path\" ] || continue\n\n  effective_config=\"${tmp_dir}/effective-$(printf '%s' \"$tsconfig_path\" | tr '/.' '__').json\"\n  showconfig_note=\n  if [ \"$has_tsc\" = \"true\" ]; then\n    if ! (cd \"$project_abs\" && tsc --showConfig -p \"$tsconfig_path\") >\"$effective_config\" 2>\"${tmp_dir}/tsc-showconfig-error.txt\"; then\n      showconfig_note=\"tsc --showConfig failed; fell back to raw tsconfig: $(cat \"${tmp_dir}/tsc-showconfig-error.txt\")\"\n      if ! strip_json_comments \"${project_abs}/${tsconfig_path}\" | jq '.' >\"$effective_config\" 2>\"${tmp_dir}/tsconfig-parse-error.txt\"; then\n        jq -n --arg path \"$tsconfig_path\" --arg rationale \"$(cat \"${tmp_dir}/tsconfig-parse-error.txt\")\" '\n          {\n            path: $path,\n            settings: [\n              {\n                name: \"tsconfig\",\n                status: \"error\",\n                category: \"type-safety\",\n                rationale: $rationale\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        ' >>\"$tsconfig_items\"\n        continue\n      fi\n    fi\n  else\n    if ! strip_json_comments \"${project_abs}/${tsconfig_path}\" | jq '.' >\"$effective_config\" 2>\"${tmp_dir}/tsconfig-parse-error.txt\"; then\n      jq -n --arg path \"$tsconfig_path\" --arg rationale \"$(cat \"${tmp_dir}/tsconfig-parse-error.txt\")\" '\n        {\n          path: $path,\n          settings: [\n            {\n              name: \"tsconfig\",\n              status: \"error\",\n              category: \"type-safety\",\n              rationale: $rationale\n            },\n            {\n              name: \"tsc\",\n              status: \"error\",\n              category: \"type-safety\",\n              rationale: \"tsc not found; effective config and migration scopes unavailable.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ' >>\"$tsconfig_items\"\n      continue\n    fi\n  fi\n\n  settings_items=\"${tmp_dir}/settings-$(printf '%s' \"$tsconfig_path\" | tr '/.' '__').jsonl\"\n  : >\"$settings_items\"\n  for setting in strict noUncheckedIndexedAccess erasableSyntaxOnly; do\n    setting_enabled=$(jq -r --arg setting \"$setting\" '.compilerOptions[$setting] == true' \"$effective_config\")\n    if [ \"$setting_enabled\" = \"true\" ]; then\n      jq -n --arg name \"$setting\" '\n        {\n          name: $name,\n          status: \"enabled\",\n          category: \"type-safety\",\n          rationale: \"\"\n        }\n      ' >>\"$settings_items\"\n    else\n      migration_scope_json=null\n      if [ \"$has_tsc\" = \"true\" ]; then\n        migration_scope=$(\n          (cd \"$project_abs\" && tsc -p \"$tsconfig_path\" \"--${setting}\" --noEmit --pretty false 2>&1 | grep -c 'error TS') || true\n        )\n        case \"$migration_scope\" in\n          ''|*[!0-9]*) migration_scope=0 ;;\n        esac\n        migration_scope_json=$migration_scope\n      fi\n\n      rationale=$(setting_rationale \"$setting\")\n      if [ -n \"$showconfig_note\" ]; then\n        rationale=\"${rationale} ${showconfig_note}\"\n      fi\n\n      jq -n \\\n        --arg name \"$setting\" \\\n        --arg rationale \"$rationale\" \\\n        --argjson migration_scope \"$migration_scope_json\" '\n          {\n            name: $name,\n            status: \"missing\",\n            category: \"type-safety\",\n            rationale: $rationale\n          }\n          + (if $migration_scope == null then {} else {migration_scope: $migration_scope} end)\n      ' >>\"$settings_items\"\n    fi\n  done\n\n  if [ \"$has_tsc\" != \"true\" ]; then\n    jq -n '\n      {\n        name: \"tsc\",\n        status: \"error\",\n        category: \"type-safety\",\n        rationale: \"tsc not found; effective config and migration scopes unavailable.\"\n      }\n    ' >>\"$settings_items\"\n  fi\n\n  jq -s --arg path \"$tsconfig_path\" '{path: $path, settings: .}' \"$settings_items\" >>\"$tsconfig_items\"\ndone <\"$tsconfig_list\"\n\ntsconfig_findings=\"${tmp_dir}/tsconfig-findings.json\"\njq -s '.' \"$tsconfig_items\" >\"$tsconfig_findings\"\n\nconfig_path_json=null\nif [ -n \"$config_path\" ]; then\n  config_path_json=$(json_string \"$config_path\")\nfi\n\nemit_report \"ok\" \"oxlint\" \"$config_path_json\" \"$oxlint_findings\" \"$tsconfig_findings\" \"$type_aware\" \"null\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
