ase4.4-tasks.md:17:- **Quote:** \"Produces: `skills/lint-audit/rules.json` -- array of rule objects with canonical names, categories, severities, default status, rationale\"\nopenspec/changes/lint-audit-skill/mission/briefs/task-1.md:1:# Worker Brief: Task 1 - Create rules.json agent-friendly ruleset\nopenspec/changes/lint-audit-skill/mission/briefs/task-1.md:5:Create `skills/lint-audit/rules.json` -- a machine-parseable JSON file defining the recommended agent-friendly oxlint ruleset. This is the data layer that `audit.sh` (Task 2) will read to compare against a project's oxlint config.\nopenspec/changes/lint-audit-skill/mission/briefs/task-1.md:25:Building a `/lint-audit` darkfactory skill that audits TypeScript projects' oxlint and tsconfig configs against agent-friendly rules. This rules.json is the source of truth for what rules the skill recommends.\nopenspec/changes/lint-audit-skill/mission/briefs/task-1.md:46:- Task 2 (audit.sh) reads rules.json with jq to compare against the project's oxlint config. Minimum integration test: `jq '.rules | length' skills/lint-audit/rules.json` returns a number >= 8.\nopenspec/changes/lint-audit-skill/mission/briefs/task-1.md:53:- Create the directory `skills/lint-audit/` if it does not exist\nopenspec/changes/lint-audit-skill/mission/briefs/task-1.md:54:- Create `skills/lint-audit/rules.json` with the ruleset\nopenspec/changes/lint-audit-skill/mission/briefs/task-1.md:56:- Commit all changes in a single commit with message: \"[task-1] Create rules.json agent-friendly ruleset\"\nopenspec/changes/lint-audit-skill/mission/briefs/task-1.md:57:- Write your handoff report to openspec/changes/lint-audit-skill/mission/handoffs/task-1.md\nopenspec/changes/lint-audit-skill/mission/briefs/task-1.md:60:- Task: Task 1 - Create rules.json agent-friendly ruleset\nopenspec/changes/lint-audit-skill/specs/ruleset-audit/spec.md:3:### Requirement: Compare oxlint rules against agent-friendly ruleset\nopenspec/changes/lint-audit-skill/specs/ruleset-audit/spec.md:4:The skill SHALL compare the project's oxlint configuration against the recommended agent-friendly ruleset defined in RULES.md.\nopenspec/changes/lint-audit-skill/specs/ruleset-audit/spec.md:7:- **WHEN** an agent-friendly rule (e.g., `typescript/no-explicit-any`) is set to `\"error\"` or `\"warn\"` in the oxlint config\nopenspec/changes/lint-audit-skill/specs/ruleset-audit/spec.md:11:- **WHEN** an agent-friendly rule is not present in the oxlint config\nopenspec/changes/lint-audit-skill/specs/ruleset-audit/spec.md:15:- **WHEN** an agent-friendly rule is set to `\"off\"` or `\"allow\"` in the oxlint config\nopenspec/changes/lint-audit-skill/specs/ruleset-audit/spec.md:20:- **THEN** the skill checks each agent-friendly rule against oxlint's default configuration and reports which are covered by defaults and which require explicit config\nopenspec/changes/lint-audit-skill/specs/ruleset-audit/spec.md:22:### Requirement: Define RULES.md schema for agent-friendly ruleset\nskills/arch-review/SKILL.md:9:Surface architectural friction and propose **deepening opportunities** — refactors that turn shallow modules into deep ones. The aim is testability and AI-navigability.\nskills/arch-review/SKILL.md:43:Then use the Agent tool with `subagent_type=Explore` to walk the codebase. Don't follow rigid heuristics — explore organically and note where you experience friction:\nskills/arch-review/SKILL.md:58:- **Problem** — why the current architecture is causing friction\nskills/arch-review/SKILL.md:64:**ADR conflicts**: if a candidate contradicts an existing ADR, only surface it when the friction is real enough to warrant revisiting the ADR. Mark it clearly (e.g. _\"contradicts ADR-0007 — but worth reopening because…\"_). Don't list every theoretical refactor an ADR forbids.\nopenspec/changes/lint-audit-skill/mission/progress.md:1:# Mission: lint-audit-skill\nopenspec/changes/lint-audit-skill/mission/handoffs/task-1.md:6:- [rules.json](/Users/stuart/.darkfactory/skil